<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ c.name }} ({{ c.ticker }}): {{ n.headline }}</title>
<style>{{ css }}</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ====================== Page 1 ====================== -->
<div class="masthead">
  <div class="house">SaaS Valuation Engine · Equity Research<small>US Software · Initiation of coverage</small></div>
  <div class="meta"><b>{{ c.name }} ({{ c.ticker }})</b><br>{{ date_long }}</div>
</div>

<div class="front">
  <main>
    <div class="kicker">{{ profile }} · Initiating at {{ t.rating }}</div>
    <h1>{{ n.headline }}</h1>
    <p class="summary">{{ n.summary }}</p>
    <div class="thesis">
      {% for p in n.thesis %}
      <div class="pillar"><h3>{{ p.title }}</h3><p>{{ p.text }}</p></div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <figure class="front-chart">{{ svg.price }}<figcaption>Source: {{ sources.price }}</figcaption></figure>
  </main>
  <aside class="sidebar">
    <div class="rating {{ t.rating }}">
      <div class="label">Rating</div><div class="value">{{ t.rating }}</div>
    </div>
    <table class="kv">
      <caption>Price target</caption>
      <tr class="strong"><td>12-month target</td><td>{{ fmt.money(t.price_target) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Share price ({{ price_date }})</td><td>{{ fmt.price(t.price) }}</td></tr>
      <tr class="strong"><td>Expected return</td><td>{{ fmt.pct(t.expected_return, signed=True) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Bull case</td><td>{{ fmt.money(t.bull_target) }} ({{ fmt.pct(t.bull_return, signed=True) }})</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Bear case</td><td>{{ fmt.money(t.bear_target) }} ({{ fmt.pct(t.bear_return, signed=True) }})</td></tr>
    </table>
    {% if t.outlier %}
    <div class="flag"><b>Model outlier.</b> The target implies a move beyond ±{{ fmt.pct(outlier_band) }}.
      Read with the valuation discussion, which explains the driver.</div>
    {% endif %}
    <table class="kv">
      <caption>Key data</caption>
      <tr><td>Market cap</td><td>{{ fmt.big(row.market_cap) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Enterprise value</td><td>{{ fmt.big(row.enterprise_value) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>52-week range</td><td>{{ fmt.money(w52[0]) }}–{{ fmt.money(w52[1]) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>EV / revenue (CY{{ cy }})</td><td>{{ fmt.mult(row.ev_revenue) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>EV / EBITDA (CY{{ cy }})</td><td>{{ fmt.mult(row.ev_ebitda) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>P / FCF (CY{{ cy }})</td><td>{{ fmt.mult(row.p_fcf) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Revenue growth (CY{{ cy }})</td><td>{{ fmt.pct(row.revenue_growth) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>FCF margin (CY{{ cy }})</td><td>{{ fmt.pct(row.fcf_margin) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Growth price implies</td><td>{{ fmt.pct(dcf.market_implied_growth) }}</td></tr>
    </table>
    <table class="kv">
      <caption>Valuation</caption>
      <tr><td>DCF value</td><td>{{ fmt.money(t.dcf_value) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Comps value</td><td>{{ fmt.money(t.comps_value) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>WACC</td><td>{{ fmt.pct(dcf.wacc, decimals=1) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Terminal growth</td><td>{{ fmt.pct(tg, decimals=1) }}</td></tr>
    </table>
  </aside>
</div>

<!-- ====================== Business and financials ====================== -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>Business overview</h2>
<p>{{ n.business_overview }}</p>

<h2>Financial summary</h2>
<table class="data">
  <tr><th>{{ "USD millions" }}</th>{% for col in fin.columns %}<th class="{{ 'est' if col.est }}">{{ col.label }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
  {% for r in fin.rows %}
  <tr class="{{ 'sub' if r.sub }}"><td>{{ r.label }}</td>{% for v in r.cells %}<td class="{{ 'est' if fin.columns[loop.index0].est }}">{{ v }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="note">Actuals are fiscal years from 10-K filings (SEC EDGAR). Estimates (E, shaded) are calendar years from the
DCF projection; estimated free cash flow is after stock-based pay, which the model treats as a cost. n/a: not in the SEC's standardized data.</p>

<div class="two">
  <figure>{{ svg.revenue }}<figcaption>Source: {{ sources.revenue }}</figcaption></figure>
  <figure>{{ svg.margins }}<figcaption>Source: {{ sources.margins }}</figcaption></figure>
</div>
<div class="two">
  <figure>{{ svg.fcf }}<figcaption>Source: {{ sources.fcf }}</figcaption></figure>
  <figure>{{ svg.comps }}<figcaption>Source: {{ sources.comps }}</figcaption></figure>
</div>

<!-- ====================== Valuation ====================== -->
<h2>Valuation and price target</h2>
<p>{{ n.valuation }}</p>
<figure>{{ svg.football_field }}<figcaption>Source: {{ sources.football_field }}</figcaption></figure>
<div class="avoid-break">
<h3>DCF sensitivity: value per share by WACC (rows) and terminal growth (columns)</h3>
<table class="data sens">
  <tr><th>WACC</th>{% for g in sens.growths %}<th>{{ fmt.pct(g, decimals=1) }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
  {% for row_ in sens.rows %}
  <tr><td><b>{{ fmt.pct(row_.rate, decimals=1) }}</b></td>
    {% for cell in row_.cells %}<td class="{{ cell.cls }}">{{ fmt.money(cell.value) }}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="note">Bordered cell: base case. Blue: above today's price of {{ fmt.price(t.price) }}; red: below.</p>
</div>

<!-- ====================== Risks ====================== -->
<h2>Risks to our rating</h2>
<ul class="risks">
  {% for r in n.risks %}<li><b>{{ r.title }}.</b> {{ r.text }}</li>{% endfor %}
</ul>
<h2>What would change our view</h2>
<ul class="watch">{% for w in n.what_would_change %}<li>{{ w }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>

<!-- ====================== Methodology and disclosures ====================== -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>Methodology</h2>
<div class="method">
  <p><b>Price target.</b> Fair value today blends a discounted cash flow value ({{ fmt.pct(m.dcf_weight) }}) with a
  comparable-company value ({{ fmt.pct(m.comps_weight) }}); where the DCF is not meaningful, the comps value is used
  alone. The 12-month target rolls fair value forward over {{ m.horizon }} months at the cost of equity less a dividend
  yield of {{ fmt.pct(m.dividend_yield) }}, rounded to the nearest dollar.</p>
  <p><b>DCF.</b> A two-stage model: {{ m.explicit }} explicit years followed by {{ m.fade }} fade years in which revenue
  growth glides to a terminal rate of {{ fmt.pct(tg, decimals=1) }} and the free-cash-flow margin moves to a mature
  level of at least {{ fmt.pct(m.target_margin) }}. Stock-based compensation is deducted as a real cost. The discount
  rate is the WACC, with the cost of equity from CAPM (risk-free rate {{ fmt.pct(m.rf, decimals=1) }}, equity risk premium
  {{ fmt.pct(m.erp, decimals=1) }}, Blume-adjusted beta).</p>
  <p><b>Comparables.</b> ln(EV/revenue) is regressed on calendar-year revenue growth across the {{ m.n }}-company
  coverage universe (R² {{ "%.2f"|format(m.r2) }}). Each company's fair multiple comes from a line fitted on the other
  companies (leave-one-out), applied to its revenue and bridged to equity value per share.</p>
  <p><b>Scenarios.</b> Bull and bear cases shift the DCF's starting growth by {{ m.growth_shift }} and its mature margin by
  {{ m.margin_shift }}, and move the fair multiple by one standard deviation of the regression residuals
  ({{ "%.2f"|format(m.resid_sd) }} in log terms, a factor of {{ "%.2f"|format(m.resid_factor) }}).</p>
  <p><b>Rating.</b> {{ m.rating_text }} Targets implying a move beyond ±{{ fmt.pct(outlier_band) }} are flagged as
  model outliers rather than capped.</p>
  <p><b>Narrative.</b> Written by {{ m.model }} from the model's figures, the company's latest 10-K (Item 1 and
  Item 1A) and a risk summary. Every number in the text was checked automatically against those sources; the rating and
  target were set by the model and given to the writer as facts.</p>
</div>
<div class="disclosures">
  <p><b>Disclosures.</b> This report was generated automatically by the SaaS Valuation Engine, an educational
  portfolio project. It is not investment research from a regulated firm and not investment advice; nothing in it is a
  recommendation to buy, sell or hold any security. Data: SEC EDGAR filings and Yahoo Finance market data as of
  {{ price_date }}. Figures may contain errors; verify against the company's filings before relying on them.</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>
